            <ArticleTitle>[Relaparotomy after emergency surgical interventions].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Relaparotomy was conducted 251 times on 210 emergency surgical patients. Diffuse and localized circumscribed peritonitis were the main causes of relaparotomy (70.5%). The level of serum cortisol was tested by the radioisotope method in a group of patients before and after relaparotomy. Operations conducted for the second time 6-7 days after the first operation were undertaken in adrenal insufficiency. Radical relaparotomy produced the best results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
